::: {.notes}
Chapter 4 introduces dynamics into the syntrometric edifice. Static colimit diagrams cannot explain why a system evolves or interacts. Heim's Enyphanie is the intrinsic capacity for transformation, measured by the scalar Enyphaniegrad g_E, acting over the 4-dimensional Syntrixtotalität T0 generated by the Protyposis (SM Eq. 14).
:::

