## §4.2.1: Principal Gauge Bundles, Functor $\Gnabla$ & Wilson Loops {.smaller}

<div class="stratum-badge badge-a">STRATUM A: PRINCIPAL CONNECTIONS (DEF. 4.1, CONST. 4.2) &amp; GAUGE INVARIANCE (PROP. 4.4)</div>

:::: {.columns}

::: {.column width="48%"}

::: {.thm-box}
**Def. 4.1 & Construction 4.2: Functor $\Gnabla \colon \Ctx \to \BunConn$**
Fix a compact Lie group $G \hookrightarrow \mathrm{O}(k)$ with Lie algebra $\mathfrak{g} \subset \mathfrak{so}(k)$ and $\Ad(G)$-invariant trace metric $\langle X, Y \rangle_{\mathfrak{g}} \coloneqq -\frac{1}{2}\tr(XY)$. For each context $U$, set $M_U \coloneqq \operatorname{Ball}(P^U)$ and $P_U \coloneqq M_U \times G$:
$$
\omega_U(x)(v) \coloneqq \Theta_U\!\Big( K^U\big(\zeta^U(d_0^U) \otimes v\big) \Big) \in \mathfrak{g}, \qquad \mathbf{A}_U(x,g)(v,\xi_g) \coloneqq \Ad(g^{-1})\omega_U(x)(v) + g^{-1}dg(\xi_g)
$$
Every context morphism $\alpha \colon V \to U$ induces a contractive bundle morphism satisfying $h_P^* \mathbf{A}_U = \mathbf{A}_V$.
:::

::: {.carnap-box .fragment}
**Def. 4.3 & Proposition 4.4: Exact Gauge Invariance of $\|F_A\|_{g_E, \mathfrak{g}}$**
The horizontal curvature $\widetilde{F}_A = d\mathbf{A} + \frac{1}{2}[\mathbf{A}, \mathbf{A}]$ descends to $F_A \in \Omega^2(M_U, \ad P_U)$. For every vertical gauge transformation $\sigma \in \mathcal{G}(P_U) \cong \Gamma(M_U, \Ad P_U)$:
$$
\|F_{\sigma \cdot A}\|_{g_E, \mathfrak{g}}^2 = \frac{1}{2}g_E^{ia}g_E^{jb}\big\langle \Ad(\sigma)F_{ij},\, \Ad(\sigma)F_{ab}\big\rangle_{\mathfrak{g}} = \|F_A\|_{g_E, \mathfrak{g}}^2
$$
:::

:::

::: {.column width="52%"}

