::: {#brst-pane-1 .syn-tab-pane .active}
**1. Normalized Yang–Mills Functional & Stationary Equation (Def. 4.8)**
$$
\mathcal{I}(\mathbf{A}) \;\coloneqq\; \frac{1}{2}\int_{M_U} \|F_A\|_{g_E, \mathfrak{g}}^2\,d\operatorname{vol}_{g_U} \;=\; -\frac{1}{4}\int_{M_U} \tr\big(F_A \wedge *F_A\big)
$$
Varying along $a \in \Omega^1(M_U, \ad P_U)$ via $\left.\frac{d}{dt}F_{A+ta}\right|_{t=0} = D_A a$ yields the stationary critical point equation:
$$
\delta\mathcal{I}_{\mathbf{A}}(a) = \int_{M_U} \langle a, D_A^* F_A \rangle\,d\operatorname{vol}_{g_U} = 0 \;\Longleftrightarrow\; D_A^* F_A = 0
$$
:::

::: {#brst-pane-2 .syn-tab-pane}
**2. Graded Configuration Algebra $\Fext$ & BRST Differential (Prop. 4.9)**
With ghost numbers $\operatorname{gh}(\mathbf{A})=0$, $\operatorname{gh}(c)=+1$, $\operatorname{gh}(\bar{c})=-1$, $\operatorname{gh}(b)=0$ and total parity $|X| = \deg_\Omega(X) + \operatorname{gh}(X) \pmod 2$:
$$
\sBRST \mathbf{A} = D_A c, \qquad \sBRST c = -\frac{1}{2}[c, c], \qquad \sBRST \bar{c} = b, \qquad \sBRST b = 0
$$
:::

::: {#brst-pane-3 .syn-tab-pane}
**3. Explicit Algebraic Cancellation of $\sBRST^2 \equiv 0$ (Bianchi + Graded Jacobi)**
$$
\begin{aligned}
\sBRST^2 c &= -\frac{1}{2}\big([\sBRST c, c] - [c, \sBRST c]\big) = \frac{1}{2}[[c, c], c] \equiv 0 \\
\sBRST^2 \mathbf{A} &= d(\sBRST c) + [\sBRST \mathbf{A}, c] - [\mathbf{A}, \sBRST c] = [[\mathbf{A}, c], c] + \frac{1}{2}[\mathbf{A}, [c, c]] \equiv 0
\end{aligned}
$$
and $\sBRST^2 \bar{c} = \sBRST b = 0$ (**Claim Ceiling $c_{\mathrm{BRST}}$**).
:::

::: {#brst-pane-4 .syn-tab-pane}
**4. Ghost-Number-Zero Physical Observable Cohomology (Fig. 4.5)**
$$
\mathcal{H}_{\mathrm{phys}} \;\cong\; H^0_{\mathrm{BRST}}(\Fext) \;=\; \frac{\ker\big(\sBRST \colon \mathcal{F}^0 \to \mathcal{F}^1\big)}{\im\big(\sBRST \colon \mathcal{F}^{-1} \to \mathcal{F}^0\big)}
$$
Quotients out unphysical longitudinal gauge modes ($\im \sBRST$) from gauge-invariant closed configurations ($\ker \sBRST$).
:::

