## §4.3.5: Pushout Functor $\YF$, Combinatorics & *Zeitkorn* $\delta t_n$ {.smaller}

<div class="stratum-badge badge-b">STRATUM B: SYNTRIXFUNKTOR COUNTS (THM. 4.18) &amp; DISCRETE CHRONOMETRY (DEFS. 4.19–4.20, FIG. 4.9)</div>

:::: {.columns}

::: {.column width="48%"}

::: {.thm-box}
**Theorem 4.18: Combinatorial Output Counts for *Syntrixfunktoren***
For an $r$-valent *Syntrixfunktor* acting on $N$ distinct *Gebilde* ($N \ge r$, SM p. 76):
$$
Z_{\mathrm{sym}} = \binom{N}{r}, \qquad Z_{k\text{-asym}} = k!\binom{N}{r}\binom{r}{k}\;\;(0 \le k \le r), \qquad Z_{\mathrm{asym}} = r!\binom{N}{r} = \frac{N!}{(N-r)!}
$$
(For $N < r$, the functor can operate only homometrally).
:::

::: {.carnap-box .fragment}
**Definitions 4.19 & 4.20: Pushout Functor $\YF$ & *Zeitkorn* ($\delta t_n$)**
1. **Sheaf Pushout Endofunctor:** On $\mathbf{Sh}(\Msyn, \mathbf{Vect}_{\mathbb{R}})$, $\YF(\mathfrak{f}) \coloneqq B \amalg_{C_0} \mathfrak{f}^{\otimes r}$.
2. **Clock-Assigned Discrete Chronometry (Fig. 4.9):** Under $\mathfrak{f}_n \coloneqq (\YF)^n(\mathfrak{f}_0)$ and strictly increasing clock $\tau \colon \mathbb{N}_0 \to \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$ ($\tau(0)=0$), the **Time Granule (*Zeitkorn*)** is:
$$
\delta t_n \;\coloneqq\; \tau(n+1) - \tau(n) > 0, \qquad t_N = \sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \delta t_k = \tau(N)
$$
:::

:::

