::: {.thm-box .fragment}
**Definition 4.23: Stabilized Affinity Bilinear Interface ($\beta^\infty$, SM Eqs. 19, 19a)**
For $\beta \in \prod_{\gamma=0}^K \prod_{\lambda=1}^L \operatorname{Bil}_{\le 1}(F_\gamma(\mathcal{S}), \mathcal{B}; \mathbb{R})$ stabilizing as $\lim_{n\to\infty}\|\beta^{(n)} - \beta^\infty\|_{\op} = 0$, the induced maps $T_\beta \colon F_0 \to \mathcal{B}^*$ and $S_\beta \colon \mathcal{B} \to F_0^*$ define an **Affinitätssyntrix Interface** iff two-sided non-degenerate on the Metrophor base $F_0 \cong P^U$:
$$
\ker T_\beta = \{0\} \quad\text{and}\quad \ker S_\beta = \{0\}
$$
:::

:::

::: {.column width="48%"}
### Compile-Ready Lean 4 Blueprint (`GaugeCurvature`, App. C)

<div class="lean-code-card">
<pre style="margin:0;"><code>import Mathlib
namespace Syntrometrie.StratumB.GaugeCurvature

/-- Background-normalized Yang-Mills coupling emergence functional (Def. 4.13) -/
def couplingEmergence2 (I_A0 I_A1 I_A2 I_total : ℝ) : ℝ :=
  I_total - (I_A1 + I_A2) + I_A0

/-- Vanishes identically when constituents decouple on curved background A₀ -/
theorem couplingEmergence2_zero_of_decoupled (I_A0 I_A1 I_A2 : ℝ) :
    couplingEmergence2 I_A0 I_A1 I_A2 (I_A1 + I_A2 - I_A0) = 0 := by
  unfold couplingEmergence2
  ring

/-- Bogomolny instanton action lower bound (Thm. 4.15) -/
theorem bogomolny_action_lower_bound (norm_sd_sq pi_sq Q_top : ℝ)
    (h_norm : 0 ≤ norm_sd_sq) :
    4 * pi_sq * Q_top ≤ (1 / 4) * norm_sd_sq + 4 * pi_sq * Q_top := by
  linarith

end Syntrometrie.StratumB.GaugeCurvature</code></pre>
</div>

::: {.intuition-box .fragment}
**Why Two-Sided Non-Degeneracy Matters:**
$\ker T_\beta = \{0\}$ ensures no internal Metrophor channel is blind to the environment $\mathcal{B}$, while $\ker S_\beta = \{0\}$ ensures no external stimulus channel is silently annihilated.
:::

:::

::::

::: {.notes}
Theorem 4.22 classifies the 3x3 transformation grid A_ik: classes A_12 and A_22 alter tensor rank and compress or inflate state-space dimension, producing topological singularities, whereas isogonal classes A_31, A_32, A_33 and field-intrinsic classes A_13, A_23 are unconditionally regular.
:::

